  "description": "SRP6a as ESP-IDF's esp_srp.c computes it for protocomm security 2: RFC 5054's 3,072-bit group (g = 5), SHA-512 as H. Salt and verifier from esp_srp_gen_salt_verifier (16-byte salt): x = H(salt | H(username ':' password)), verifier = g^x mod N, in its minimal big-endian bytes. k = H(N | PAD(g)). The client's A = g^a mod N is sent as 384 bytes. The board's B = (k v + g^b) mod N, in its minimal bytes (so 383 when its first byte would be zero), with b of 32 bytes. u = H(PAD(A) | PAD(B)), each padded to 384 bytes. S = (A v^u)^b = (B - k g^x)^(a + u x) mod N, and sessionKey K = H(S) over S's minimal bytes. clientProof M = H((H(N) xor H(PAD(g))) | H(username) | salt | A | B | K), with A and B exactly as sent; deviceProof = H(A | M | K). Private values are big-endian. Made by running ESP-IDF's own code as the board, with these fixed values, against a second client whose proofs that code accepted; each case also names the property it pins.",
  "source": "ESP-IDF v6.1.1 (commit 051e4c4eb20346e043cdd47bc388fde75ff8af63): components/protocomm/src/security/security2.c, src/common/protocomm.c, src/crypto/srp6a/esp_srp.c and esp_srp_mpi.c, proto-c/*.pb-c.c; protobuf-c 1.4.1 (commit abc67a11c6db271bedbb9f58be85d6f4e2ea8389); Mbed TLS 4.1.1 with TF-PSA-Crypto (commit ce3f3485a121c100f58f36d700cb35b060f6e866). Compiled for the host and run by packages/protocol/src/pairing/esp-idf/make-vectors.sh",
